  <h2>🚫 2. Universal Negativ Prompt (Taqiqlangan Elementlar)</h2>
  <p>Istalgan generatsiyada quyidagi qatorni negativ maydonga qo‘shing:</p>
  <code>negative prompt: cartoon, 3d render, illustration, fake smile, studio lighting, posed plastic model, generic stock photo, corporate wear, oversaturated unnatural colors, clean polished city clothes, blurred unrecognizable background, bad anatomy, deformed limbs, blurry low-res artifacts, watermarks, bad lettering.</code>

  <h2>⚡ 3. Beshta Mustaqil Grafik Poster Stili</h2>

  <h3>🧗 STIL 1: GORPCORE TECHNICAL EDITORIAL</h3>
  <p><strong>Konseptsiya:</strong> Salomon Advanced va Arc'teryx jurnallari uslubidagi yuqori darajadagi texnik plakat.<br>
  <strong>Asosiy Elementlar:</strong> Sayohatchi yuzida/harakatida gorizontal shutter motion blur, texnik xantal-sariq kurtka, Shveytsar spec-sheet GPS gridi, baquvvat sans-serif sarlavha, telemetriya va pastki falsafiy matn bloki.</p>
  <code>A finished high-end gorpcore technical editorial graphic design poster for "[DESTINATION / TOUR NAME]". A lone athletic hiker scrambling powerfully through rugged granite boulders and dense mountain woods in [LOCATION]. Intentional dynamic horizontal shutter drag motion blur across the subject's face and hands conveying intense physical exertion. The hiker wears a technical mustard yellow weatherproof shell jacket, dark utility cargo pants, and a technical trekking pack. Integrated modern Swiss graphic design poster layout: massive bold white condensed sans-serif typography across the top reading "[MAIN HEADLINE]", complemented by crisp white technical typography overlay with GPS coordinates "[COORDINATES]", "ELEVATION [ALTITUDE]M", crosshair vector marks, technical spec barcode, and an elegant small editorial text block at the bottom discussing human endurance and wilderness solitude. Muted forest green, slate rock, and sharp mustard yellow palette, raw analog 35mm photography texture, sharp typography layout, award-winning editorial poster design. --ar 4:5 --style raw</code>

  <h3>🏃 STIL 2: YOUTH COMMUNITY & KINETIC BLUR</h3>
  <p><strong>Konseptsiya:</strong> Yoshlarbop outdoor klubi, erkin harakat va jamoaviy sayohatlar afishasi.<br>
  <strong>Asosiy Elementlar:</strong> Ko‘p qatlamli premium kinetik blur (oyoq-qo‘llar va fonda harakat surkalishi), oltin soat quyosh nurlari, dinamik jamoa, erkin suyuq qabariq (liquid/puffy) retro sarlavha (sarlavha istalgan nomga moslashadi!).</p>
  
  <p><em>Kunduzgi Jamoa & Suyuq Retro Sarlavha:</em></p>
  <code>A finished vibrant outdoor community graphic design poster titled "[YOUR CUSTOM HEADLINE]". An energetic, diverse crew of young stylish friends moving joyfully along a scenic mountain trail through lush groves in [LOCATION]. Lead person holds a waving outdoor club flag. Strong premium kinetic shutter motion blur across running legs, swinging arms, and edges, with sharp joyful facial expressions. Warm golden hour cinematic sunlight filtering through trees. Graphic design poster elements: large fluid puffy liquid retro typography arched across the top displaying "[YOUR CUSTOM HEADLINE]" in warm cream and adventure orange. Lower section features a circular vector community badge, small clean typography with meetup details: "[DATE] • [DEPARTURE POINT] • [PRICE]", analog 35mm film flash aesthetic, infectious youthful freedom, modern running club poster. --ar 4:5 --style raw</code>

  <p><em>Tungi Neon Blur & Roof Cinema:</em></p>
  <code>A finished dark atmospheric cinema and night-trail graphic event poster set in [LOCATION]. High-speed runner captured mid-stride with intense artistic motion blur and light streaks against dark pine silhouettes. Centered with a blazing electric neon orange glowing blurred typography reading "[YOUR CUSTOM HEADLINE]", with chromatic aberration and lens flare. Lower section features a clean minimalist graphic data card: "[DATE & TIME] • [PRICE] • OUTDOOR CINEMA & BONFIRE", small neon cyan badge, raw 35mm film grain, futuristic dark gorpcore aesthetic, high impact graphic design. --ar 4:5 --style raw</code>

  <h3>🧵 STIL 3: ORIENTAL TEXTILE & SWISS BRUTALISM</h3>
  <p><strong>Konseptsiya:</strong> An'anaviy Sharq/O‘zbek gilami to‘qimasi bilan zamonaviy Shveytsar brutalist grafika sintezi.<br>
  <strong>Asosiy Elementlar:</strong> Giper-realistik an'anaviy gilam/palos to‘qimasi foni, pikselli 8-bit sarlavha, qat'iy oq-qora turlar jadvali, shtrix-kodlar va texnik krestiklar.</p>
  <code>A striking graphic design tour poster fusing traditional Central Asian oriental carpet craftsmanship with modern Swiss brutalist tour poster typography. The entire background is a hyper-detailed tactile macro texture of an antique handwoven oriental wool rug with rich burgundy, indigo, and terracotta tribal motifs. Centered on top of the carpet is an uncompromising brutalist data layout: massive pixelated 8-bit black-letter headline reading "[DESTINATION / TOUR NAME]", overlaid with a stark white and black data grid box displaying schedule details: "[DATE] — [TOUR NAME] / ELEV: [ALTITUDE]M", "DIFFICULTY: ★ ★ ★ ☆ ☆", "PRICE: [PRICE]", complete with graphic barcodes, technical crosshairs, and a small high-contrast black-and-white photo print of a hiker taped to the layout. Bold contemporary graphic design, high-contrast cultural synthesis, sharp typography on vintage textile. --ar 4:5 --style raw</code>

  <h3>🎬 STIL 4: RETRO ALPINE CINEMA & GRAPHIC SUNBURST</h3>
  <p><strong>Konseptsiya:</strong> 1970-yillar sarguzasht filmlari va kinofestival afishasi estetikasi.<br>
  <strong>Asosiy Elementlar:</strong> Qorli cho‘qqi orqasida qalin geometrik qizil-to‘q-sariq quyosh nurlari (sunburst), 70-yillar vintage serif sarlavhasi, pastda kinofilm billing-bloki (titrlar).</p>
  <code>A vintage 1970s adventure cinema graphic poster titled "[DESTINATION NAME]". In the center, a dramatic rocky mountain peak and pine tree ridgeline of [LOCATION], silhouetted against an epic bold geometric sunburst of radiant crimson red, mustard yellow, and burnt orange graphic rays beaming across the entire sky. Top typography features a massive curved vintage film title in nostalgic 70s bold serif typography reading "[MAIN TITLE]". The bottom edge features a classic cinematic credits billing block layout: "A TASHQARIGA EXPEDITION • [DATE] • FEATURING [DISTANCE]KM TREK • SOUNDTRACK BY THE WILD", printed on aged cream paper with authentic screenprint texture, lithograph halftones, warm nostalgic Kodachrome film grading. --ar 4:5 --style raw</code>

  <h3>🗺️ STIL 5: TOPO-TRAIL & DOODLE STICKER</h3>
  <p><strong>Konseptsiya:</strong> Keng tabiat manzarasi, uning ustiga chizilgan oq GPS trail yo‘li va shoshilinch neon skotch stikerlari.<br>
  <strong>Asosiy Elementlar:</strong> Keng formatli tog‘ surati, landshaft ustidan o‘tgan oq vektor topo-marshrut chizig‘i va marra bayroqchasi, suyuq oq kontur sarlavha, burchakda neon pushti duct-tape stikeri (<em>«NEARLY GONE»</em>), pastda aniq narx va telemetriya.</p>
  <code>A high-energy mixed-media scrapbook graphic design poster for "[DESTINATION / TOUR NAME]". The base image is an awe-inspiring wide landscape photograph of [LOCATION WITH MOUNTAINS AND RIVER]. Directly overlaid onto the landscape photograph is a crisp white vector topographic trail line accurately mapping the route across the ridges ending at a checkered flag. In the top corner, a realistic semi-transparent neon hot-pink duct tape sticker is slapped at an angle, stamped with bold distressed font "[STICKER TEXT: e.g. NEARLY GONE // 179,000 UZS]". Curving gracefully along the mountain contours is liquid white outline hand-drawn typography reading "[MAIN TITLE]". At the bottom, clean technical telemetry text: "[DATE] • PRICE: [PRICE] • TASHQARIGA OUTDOOR", coordinate stamps, tactile textured cut-and-paste collage aesthetic, trendsetting modern outdoor poster. --ar 4:5 --style raw</code>

  <h2>📌 4. Amaliy Misol: "Lashkarak O‘rmoni" Tayyor Promptlari</h2>

  <p><strong>1. Gorpcore Usulida:</strong></p>
  <code>A finished high-end gorpcore technical editorial graphic design poster for "LASHKARAK JUNIPER FOREST". A lone athletic hiker scrambling powerfully through rugged granite boulders and dense alpine juniper woods in the Qurama Mountains of Uzbekistan. Intentional dynamic horizontal shutter drag motion blur across the subject's face and hands conveying intense physical exertion. The hiker wears a technical mustard yellow Arc'teryx style weatherproof shell jacket, dark utility cargo pants, and a technical trekking pack. Integrated modern Swiss graphic design poster layout: massive bold white condensed sans-serif typography across the top reading "BUILT FOR THE WILD", complemented by crisp white technical typography overlay with GPS coordinates "41°09'24\"N 70°14'15\"E", "ELEVATION 1780M - QURAMA RIDGE", "19-20 SEPTEMBER • 199,000 UZS / CLUB: 179,000 UZS", crosshair vector marks, technical spec barcode, and an elegant small editorial text block at the bottom discussing human endurance and wilderness solitude. Muted forest green, slate rock, and sharp mustard yellow palette, raw analog 35mm photography texture, sharp typography layout, award-winning editorial poster design. --ar 4:5 --style raw</code>

  <p><strong>2. Youth Kinetic Motion (Premium Blur & Dynamic Headline):</strong></p>
  <code>A finished vibrant outdoor community graphic design poster titled "LASHKARAK CREW ESCAPE". An energetic, diverse crew of young stylish friends moving joyfully along a scenic mountain trail through lush walnut groves in Lashkarak, Uzbekistan. Lead person holds a waving canvas outdoor club flag. Strong premium kinetic shutter motion blur and light drag across running legs and background, with authentic happy facial expressions. Warm golden hour cinematic sunlight filtering through trees. Graphic design poster elements: large fluid puffy liquid retro typography arched across the top displaying "LASHKARAK ESCAPE" in warm cream and adventure orange. Lower section features a circular vector community badge, clean typography with details: "19-20 SEPTEMBER • 199,000 UZS / TRAVEL CLUB: 179,000 UZS", analog 35mm film flash aesthetic, youthful freedom, modern outdoor club poster. --ar 4:5 --style raw</code>

  <p><strong>3. Topo-Trail & Sticker Usulida:</strong></p>
  <code>A finished graphic design outdoor travel poster for Lashkarak Forest expedition in Uzbekistan. The image features a lush green mountain forest with rushing river and misty peaks in the background. Prominently overlaid at the top is bold white contour outline typography that reads "LASHKARAK". Across the landscape, a hand-drawn white GPS hiking trail line curves through the trees ending at a small checkered flag. In the corner, a vibrant neon pink tape sticker reads "NEARLY GONE". At the bottom, clean technical telemetry text displays: "19-20 SEPTEMBER · 199,000 UZS / CLUB: 179,000 UZS · TASHQARIGA OUTDOOR". Trend-setting neo-gorpcore adventure poster layout, magazine editorial style, sharp graphic details, photorealistic landscape with graphic overlays. --ar 4:5 --style raw</code>

